## 8. Findings — none blocking

A1 (advise) **The 599px `:has()` rule is asserted by no test.** The brief's
   1280-only scoping is honestly stated and I accept it for this opus — a spec
   claiming three viewports without running three would be the worse fault, and
   the brief explicitly refuses to overclaim. But the scoping is not uniform in
   risk. 1280 and 800 share ONE code path (the base
   `.shell:has(.token-prompt) { grid-template-rows: auto 1fr }`), which
   behaviour 1 pins. The `max-width: 599px` block carries its OWN rule —
   `grid-template-rows: auto 48px 1fr` — and that line is exercised by nothing
   in CI. It is verified today only by this attended pass, which does not run
   again. Exactly one unasserted rule, and it is the one most likely to rot.
   Target: add 500 (and 800) to behaviour 1's describe block — the harness,
   the assertions and the loop already exist, so it is a few lines. The brief
   itself calls widening "a reasonable follow-on"; this names which viewport
   actually needs it and why.

A2 (note) **The brief's token enumeration is incomplete.** It states the
   `.token-prompt__*` rules use "tokens only — `--wash`, `--rule`, `--amber`,
   `--ink`, `--ink-2`, `--font-body`, `--font-mono`, `--sp-*`", but
   `.token-prompt__input:focus` also uses `var(--verdigris)`. That IS a defined
   token (`#0B6E5F`, pinned by apps/web/test/tokens.test.ts:33) and it matches
   the file's existing focus idiom (three other `outline: 2px solid
   var(--verdigris)` uses), so the accessibility path is correct and no hex
   literal was smuggled in. The enumeration is simply missing a name.

A3 (note) **The opus record's two spec pointers diverge.**
   `spec: briefs/W-075.md` (current spec of record) while
   `probationes.spec.evidence: opera/W-075.md` (what the architect actually
   signed at 01:52:58). Both are individually truthful and §5 explains why the
   second was deliberately left alone. But a reader of the record ALONE sees a
   spec gate certifying a document that lists no behaviours. The brief's
   opening paragraph reconciles it; nothing in the record points at that
   paragraph. Closed by W-062's `amend` verb landing, or by a line in the
   traditio.

A4 (note) **The brief's binding input is not reachable from the officina.** It
   cites "the ui-lead's (Terra's) measurement of the defect"; those screenshots
   live in a session scratchpad outside the repo, so the record cannot reach
   them. §2 of this log records the same measurement numerically, which is
   durable and tracked, so the evidence is preserved — but by this log, not by
   the brief's own citation.

A5 (note) **Second disclosed hand edit of opera front matter this week**
   (W-046's title, now W-075's spec pointer), both forced by the absent `amend`
   verb and both correctly disclosed. Two is a tracked exception; a third makes
   it a habit. W-062's priority should move on the next instance.

## 9. Verdict: PASS

The defect is real, the fix is right, and every claim the brief makes that I
could test, I tested rather than accepted:

  - the reproduction it instructs a censor to run **reproduces**, re-derived
    from master via git rather than from the builder's stash: same assertion,
    same line, Expected 0 / Received 220;
  - the coverage-gap explanation is **confirmed in source**, and the rival
    explanation I tried is **refuted by measurement**;
  - the stash mechanism is **sound** under D-024's own frame — the recorded
    base is the trunk (header `dirty:1b165057…` == master's source tree), the
    recorded state is the shipped product rather than a fabrication, and the
    proposition is reproducible by execution. This is W-046 round 3's already
    accepted shape, not a new exception, and asks for no waiver;
  - the spec-pointer hand edit is **forced** (no verb writes that field on a
    `building` opus), **minimal** (one field), **disclosed** with its reason
    and tracking opus, **load-bearing** (measured: FAIL 1 blocking without it,
    PASS 0 blocking with it), and preserves more truth than re-running `ready`
    would have;
  - all three breakpoints are **verified live with numbers and screenshots**;
  - `test:serve` is **17/17 from a clean rebuilt dist**, and the sixteen
    untouched specs are themselves the proof that the prompt-closed layout did
    not move.

The fix is CSS-only, `:has()`-scoped so the common case is byte-identical, and
its authority is TokenPrompt's own documented placement rather than a new
layout decision — correctly, since a ui-lead or Patron ruling would otherwise
be required and none was sought.

Five advisories (§8), none warranting a round. A1 is the only one with teeth
and it names a concrete, small follow-on.

## 10. Class findings for the retrospectio

C5  **red×reproducible-pre-fix-state** — NEW, and worth naming precisely so it
    is not confused with C1. A red recorded out of order but against the
    SHIPPED TRUNK, whose failure any third party can re-derive from the trunk
    alone. Distinct from C1 (`red×backfilled-provenance`, W-071, D-024) by one
    property: the recorded state existed as a real product. Sound as it
    stands; no waiver, no decision needed. Both classes are nevertheless
    closed by the SAME mechanism — P-012's working-tree identity would make
    this red self-describing instead of merely re-derivable, which is the
    difference between verifiable by inspection and verifiable by execution.
    Another live argument for P-012, from the accepted side of the line.

C6  **spec×written-after-the-build** — the brief is openly retrofitted to a
    CSS-only fix dispatched with its opus record as the spec, and says so in
    its first paragraph. Proportionality was the right call for a one-line
    defect; the cost was a blocking `opus.red_evidence` on the officina, paid
    later. Target: `ready`'s `--spec` default already assumes
    `briefs/<id>.md`; the cheap fix is for the record-as-spec shortcut to be
    refused up front rather than discovered by `check` after the build. Not
    this opus's to carry.

C7  **hand-edit×absent-verb** — second live instance this week (A5). Tracked,
    disclosed, forced. Target: W-062 (`amend`). Escalate on a third.

Carried, unchanged, still not this opus's: C4
(`gate×network-dependent-probatio`) — `npm test` still makes cold TLS
connections to registry.npmjs.org from ci.test.ts's genuine `npm ci` fixture.

